course: dictionary
lesson: 9766
title: Suppression: stopping something
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Suppression means stopping something, or holding it back. When you meet a new word, read the words around it. They are its context, and they leave clues about what is being stopped and how.
explain: «Some false claims about voting days are spread on purpose to stop people voting, which is called voter suppression.» The clues are stop people voting and false claims, so voter suppression means stopping people from voting, often in an unfair way.
explain: Suppression can also mean holding back a feeling, a cough or a thought, or stopping a fire from growing. Ask yourself: is something being stopped by force, held back by a person, or prevented from growing?
fact: Suppression means stopping something, or holding it back.
fact: «Suppression» can mean stopping something by force or power, such as «suppression of the rebellion» or «suppression of free speech».
fact: «Suppression» can also mean holding back a feeling, a cough, a sneeze or a thought.
fact: «Fire suppression» means stopping a fire from growing, for example with sprinklers.
fact: Suppression is an uncountable noun, so we say «some suppression», not «a suppression».
exercise: «Some false claims about voting days are spread on purpose to stop people voting, which is called voter suppression.» What is voter suppression? | Voting for the best party | *Stopping people from voting, often unfairly | Counting every vote twice | Giving everyone a free day off work
exercise: Sprinklers that stop a fire from spreading are an example of what? | a fire drill | a bonfire night | *fire suppression | a fire engine
exercise: Mia held back a sneeze in class. Which word from this lesson describes holding it back? | Explosion | Eruption | *Suppression | Invention
test: «The suppression of the rebellion took several weeks.» What does suppression mean here? | Celebrating with a parade | *Stopping the rebellion by force | Letting the rebels win | Starting a new party
test: Which sentence uses suppression correctly? | *The news report described the suppression of free speech. | We ate three suppressions for lunch. | The shop had a suppression of apples. | The suppressions ran home after school.
exam: «The doctor talked about the suppression of his cough.» Which meaning fits best? | Buying a cough sweet for the school trip | Sending the cough to the hospital | *Holding back or stopping the cough | Making the cough louder
